<title>NETHERLANDS: CSM finalises Scandinavian takeover.</title>
<headline>CSM finalises Scandinavian takeover.</headline>
<dateline>AMSTERDAM 1997-03-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Dutch food group CSM NV said on Friday it had finalised the takeover of Scandinavian sweets maker Malaco Group which was announced last June.</p>
<p>All authorities have approved the deal, which officially became effective today. The takeover sum has been paid in cash, CSM said without disclosing further details.</p>
<p>Sweden-based Malaco has factories in Sweden and Denmark and a sales organisation in Norway. The company has 780 employees and posts annual turnover of 860 million Swedish crowns or about 215 million guilders, CSM said in a statement.</p>
<p>-- Amsterdam newsroom +31 20 504 5000, Fax +31 20 504 5040</p>
